-/*
- * RMSNorm fork of the coalescing fabric forwarder
- * (dit_fused_norm_common/kernels/dataflow/dit_fused_norm_forwarder.cpp), with a two-wave mode.
- * Consumer: ttnn::experimental::prim::DitFusedDistributedRmsnormMeshWorkloadFactory only.
- *
- * num_waves == 1: the original per-row-round protocol, unchanged:
- *   per round r: wait present_count(r) arrivals, ring-multicast packet_buf[r%2] to the
- *   DRAM page (my_device, forwarder, r) on every chip fused with an atomic inc of every
- *   peer forwarder's out_ready_sem, wait the cumulative peer incs, then inc each present
- *   worker's go-sem.
- *
- * num_waves == 2 (max_rounds == 1): the group's slots are split into two waves,
- *   [wave_bound[0], wave_bound[1]) and [wave_bound[1], wave_bound[2]). The factory starts
- *   wave 1's input read only as wave 0's lands, so wave 0's ring gather overlaps wave 1's
- *   DRAM read and wave 1's gather overlaps wave 0's output drain. Each wave is counted in
- *   its own 16-bit field of the (shared) semaphores: a wave-w worker incs fwd_arrival by
- *   1 << (16*w), and wave w's fused fabric inc adds 1 << (16*w) to every peer's out_ready.
- *   So a fast peer's wave-1 inc can never satisfy this chip's wave-0 wait, and wave 1's
- *   packet doesn't have to wait behind wave 0's out_ready. Both waves share packet_buf[0]
- *   and DRAM page (my_device, forwarder, 0) at their own slot offsets, so the stats-buffer
- *   geometry and the workers' gathered-stick read (page 0 + slot*stick) are unchanged.
- *   One poll loop: send wave `sent` once its arrivals are complete; release wave
- *   `released` once all peers' wave packets have landed.
- */
